From 0f653475ff6bc75ed363ed3af5bd5d65f49699ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forklift <forklift@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:06:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] forklift: C-WM loop candidate window, feature switches
 and their refusals

FORKLIFT_SLAM_CWM_S=T starts FindPossibleLoopClosure at the first state id whose scan is
at most T sim seconds old (binary search; ids are contiguous in a fresh sync mapping) --
max(rStartNum, window start), so TryCloseLoop's repeated calls only move forward. A probed
id with no scan aborts the node (a broken premise ends the run rather than run another arm).
The configuration reads FORKLIFT_SLAM_{CWM_S,DELETE_OLDER_S,S1,S1_BUFFER}; more than one
feature at once, or any feature in a lifelong, localization, async or map-and-localization
node or on a deserialized graph, ends the node. The identification line prints them all.
gtest forklift_patch_test covers the window search.
